What is a Promissory Note Due on a Specific Date?
A Promissory Note Due on a Specific Date is a legal loan document in which the borrower promises to repay the lender in full on an agreed future date. It clearly records the loan amount, repayment deadline, interest terms, and obligations of both parties.
This type of Promissory Note Due on a Specific Date is useful when both lender and borrower want certainty about when the loan must be paid back. It creates written proof of the debt and helps avoid disputes.

